5. Can a void function take a parameter?
Yes, a void function can take parameters. The void keyword only means the function does not return a value to the caller. It can still accept input values (parameters) to perform tasks like printing or modifying global data.
• Example: void printScore(int score) { cout << score; }
6. What is a Recursive Algorithm? (Factorial Example)
A Recursive Algorithm is a method where a function calls itself to solve a problem by breaking it down into smaller sub-problems. Every recursive function must have a Base Case to stop the recursion.
Factorial Implementation:
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int factorial(int n) {
    // Base Case
    if (n <= 1) 
        return 1;
    // Recursive Call
    return n * factorial(n - 1);
}

int main() {
    int num = 5;
    cout << "Factorial of " << num << " is: " << factorial(num) << endl;
    return 0;
}
